WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.420
Jack: To make sure that we are
communicating correctly we need

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.500
to first seek feedback and not
just expect it to come to us.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:10.080
The first thing to think about
when seeking feedback is what

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.430
do we want from the feedback?

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.840
Is it to know whether the communication
was understood, was clear to everyone?

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.359
Or to be more specific, such as
getting individuals to feedback

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.959
directly with data and immediate
responses to particular questions.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.380
The things that we most commonly
seek feedback about are suitability,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.230
relevancy, and usefulness.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:33.419
We want to see if the message we were
trying to get across was received by all

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.850
and was clear, effective, and informative.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.170
Leah: So, who do we
seek that feedback from?

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.820
Within a programming environment the
other parties that we may seek feedback

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.290
from are clients with whom we may be
communicating about their new software,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:53.160
colleagues, and team members who we may
be collaborating with on a development

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:57.960
project, and managers, stakeholders,
and any third parties who may be

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.820
involved at some stage with a project.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.580
It doesn’t matter who they are,
their feedback will often help

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.210
with the process of communication.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.720
Jack: So how can we get feedback that
meets our requirements and is timely?

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.100
The person who is communicating should
set out the guidelines for feedback

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.520
and make sure that they ask for it.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:20.500
They should also make everyone aware that
feedback is an important and helpful way

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.690
of them confirming their understanding
and in turn for gaining a response.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.029
For a more

00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:29.519
Leah: efficient process they should
enable feedback to be given by means

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.320
of creating a mechanism for it.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.990
Feedback can be given by a variety of
means such as by informal and formal

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:41.100
meetings, email questioning, polls,
surveys, focus groups and questionnaires.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.710
The approach will depend on
the feedback that is wanted

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.110
and how quickly it is needed.

